GPT-QModel CPU AVX512-BF16 GPTQ kernel
=====================================

The sources in this directory are adapted from the MIT-licensed
`quantization-gptq` kernel in Hugging Face `kernels-community`:

  https://github.com/huggingface/kernels-community/tree/c467920211e144ea621d9e8193ff71ec160ce256/quantization-gptq

Original author: jiqing-feng <jiqing.feng@intel.com>

GPT-QModel changes:
  * removed the full-weight dequantization path used for M > 100, which was
    slower than the on-the-fly dequantization plus brgemm path
  * moved the tiny-GEMM/brgemm crossover from M > 4 to M > 24
  * added a fused GPTQ-to-HF int4 packer, replacing the much slower Python
    unpack/reorder/pack conversion used while loading a checkpoint; see
    `tests/benchmark/benchmark_gptq_cpu_avx512.py` for measured host-specific
    results
  * skip activation gather and packer index-select when `ret_idx` is the
    canonical identity mapping
  * registered the kernel under the `gptqmodel_gptq_cpu` torch.ops namespace
  * added tensor dtype/shape/index validation and an empty-batch fast path
  * tightened AVX512-BF16 host detection to require every ISA feature used by
    the kernel and enabled OS XSAVE state
  * size the OpenMP region from PyTorch's intra-op thread count so
    `torch.set_num_threads()` is honored when `OMP_NUM_THREADS` is unset
